  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** RMR operates a durable, multi-sector platform anchored by perpetual, long-term contracts with managed REITs and private capital clients, which shields a significant portion of revenue from cyclical pressure. Amid an unsettled economic environment marked by market volatility and geopolitical uncertainty, core fee streams held close to plan, though sequential service revenues softened due to hotel divestitures, lower enterprise values from debt paydowns at certain REITs, and the planned wind-down of a life-science business. The narrative is buoyed by a meaningful return of incentive fees from Diversified Healthcare Trust and Industrial Logistics Properties Trust, signaling underlying portfolio performance, while ongoing private capital fundraising adds a growth tailwind.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership highlighted results at or above the high end of internal outlooks and maintained the quarterly dividend, reinforcing a shareholder-return focus. The team deployed balance-sheet capacity into recent SVC and Greenwich investments, boosting liquidity to roughly $120 million, and continues to emphasize a valuation discount versus peers as a catalyst. The messaging is transparent, acknowledging a slight miss on one adjusted metric while underscoring the pipeline of incentive fees and promote potential. The steady cadence of disclosed co-investment moves and the preserved dividend signal disciplined capital allocation even in a choppy macro backdrop.",
